DECL	{"args":[{"name":"u","sort":{"sort":"track"}},{"name":"r","sort":{"sort":"region"}}],"body":{"rises":{"args":[{"var":"u"},{"var":"r"}],"atom":"rel_occupies","params":[]}},"contract":"The road user's footprint comes to overlap a structure region at the observation: it overlaps the region at the observation and did not overlap it at the observation before. The concept is the event of that coming to overlap, read at the observation at which the overlap has begun, and not the state of lying inside the region afterwards. It states no direction of entry, no carrier the road user came through, no speed and no place within the region. Not a stand-in for: lying within the region, which the occupancy relation carries on its own; a later observation at which the road user is still inside; the carrier or the way the road user came from, which a caller reads with its own relations; a crossing of a boundary the source represents by no region; or a leaving of the region.","definition":null,"id":"drv.motion.region_entry","kind":"formula","narrowings":[],"params":[],"residues":[],"supersedes":null}
